## Why This Is Asked
Assesses understanding of B2B guest access lifecycle, least-privilege, and simple automation.

## Key Concepts
- Azure AD B2B guest invites
- Group-based access to a single resource
- Conditional Access MFA for guests
- Expiration and rollback mechanisms
- Auditing and verification

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo code for revoking guest access via Graph API
async function revokeGuestAccess(guestEmail) {
  // remove from group
  await removeMemberFromGroup(guestEmail, 'Partner_SharePoint_Access');
  // clean up guest if orphaned
  await deleteGuestUserIfOrphan(guestEmail);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the expiration and rollback in a sandbox?
- What pitfalls exist with guest access and MFA coverage?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical mastery of Azure AD risk-based access controls at scale, including how to design policies, test them safely, and rollback without service disruption.

## Key Concepts

- Identity Protection risk scoring
- Conditional Access policies
- MFA and device compliance
- Session controls and continuous access evaluation
- SIEM integration and audit trails
- Safe rollback and access-review processes

## Code Example

```json
{
  "conditionalAccessPolicy": {
    "displayName": "Risk-based admin access",
    "conditions": {
      "users": { "include": ["admin@contoso.com"] },
      "signInRiskLevels": ["high","medium"],
      "platforms": { "include": ["All"] }
    },
    "grantControls": {
      "builtInControls": ["mfa","deviceCompliance"],
      "sessionControls": ["requireUserConsent","limitSessionDuration"]
    },
    "applications": ["https://portal.contoso.com/admin"]
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate these policies in a sandbox before production?
- How would you measure impact on admin productivity and detect policy drift?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical PIM/JIT implementation with governance.

## Key Concepts
- Privileged Identity Management (PIM)
- Just-In-Time (JIT) access
- Activation workflow and MFA
- Approvals, auditing, and alerts
- Emergency break-glass handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// PIM-like activation flow (illustrative)
const activate = async (roleId, user) => {
  // request activation with approval
  await graphClient.post(`/roleAssignments`, { roleDefinitionId: roleId, principalId: user });
  // MFA enforcement occurs at login/activation
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the emergency bypass path and ensure controls aren’t bypassed?
- How would you export and present an audit report of activations for compliance?
